-- title:
--   K-finiteness of vectors in the archimedean dual cut
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and let `tys` be an archimedean type family for $F$: a function assigning to each infinite place $w$ of $F$ a cardinality $\mathrm{card}\,w \in \mathbb{N}$ together with, for each index $i \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{card}\,w)$, a datum $\mathrm{rep}\,w\,i$ consisting of a natural number $n$ and a representation $\rho$ of the group `rowIsometrySubgroup₀ w.Completion` on $\mathbb{C}^n$. Let $f$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $F$, and assume $f$ belongs to the archimedean dual cut submodule `archDualCutSubmodule F tys`, that is, to the intersection over all infinite places $w$ of the sum over $i \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{card}\,w)$ of the submodules `typeSubmodule (rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w) ((tys.rep w i).ρ.dual)` attached to the group homomorphism `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w` and the dual of the representation $\rho$ of $\mathrm{rep}\,w\,i$. Then the $\mathbb{C}$-linear span of the set of all functions of the form $x \mapsto f(xk)$, where $k$ ranges over the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles generated by the ranges of the homomorphisms `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w` over all infinite places $w$ (their supremum as subgroups), is a finite-dimensional complex vector space.
--
--   This is the $K$-finiteness statement for vectors lying in the archimedean cut prescribed by the contragredients of a finite family of archimedean types: a function cut out at every infinite place by finitely many such types has a finite-dimensional span of right translates under the group generated by the archimedean row-isometry subgroups. It is used in the construction of the archimedean cut projector, through [`AutomorphicForm.exists_rightConv_eq_of_archCutProjector`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_rightConv_eq_of_archCutProjector).
